    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2NRvc1C3wMiLJubU292uu3b)_\n\n## Cause\n- The real litnotes use numbered definition footnotes: `[fn:1]` in the text and `[fn:1] ... [[id:...][Concept]]` below.\n- The scanner (PR #366) only read inline `[fn::[[id:...]]]` footnotes, so it found zero mentions and every widget and dashboard stayed empty (the reindex commands still ran, with nothing to index).\n- Checked on the real vault: 8 litnotes have 11 id-linked definitions and none has an inline see-also footnote.\n\n## Changes\n- `sp-see-also-parse-buffer` now reads definition footnotes too; context comes from the first reference, `:def-beg`/`:def-end` mark the definition.\n- PR #367 (sidenotes) uses the same parser, so it gets both forms (reference range plus definition text) with no change.\n- Cache version bumped to 2 so old empty scans are redone.\n- New interactive `sp-see-also-show` and `sp-see-also-show-concept`, which work without vui or the sidebar.\n- A failure while loading the widgets is now reported in `*Messages*` instead of being swallowed.\n- Literate doc updated (bullet lists) and tests added (20 pass; sidenote tests still pass); also run against two real litnotes.\n\n## Not verified\n- The vulpea-ui widgets themselves (no vui in the cloud container) and the real `vulpea-db-query-links-to` shape.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBMe7TUL1fNpmHTqt8)_",
